course: dictionary
lesson: 7224
title: Photographer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A photographer is a person who takes photographs. Some photographers do it as a job, and some do it as a hobby. «The school photographer took our class picture on Monday.» The sentence tells you the photographer came to school with a camera, so the word means someone whose work is taking pictures.
explain: The word can also mean the person who took one particular photo. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits. «Paparazzi are photographers who follow famous people to sell pictures.» Here the clues are follow and sell, so photographers can be people who chase others to get pictures. Chasing someone is frightening, and that is why it is not a good thing to do.
explain: Ask yourself what kind of photographer the sentence is about. «He is a wildlife photographer» tells you the job is taking pictures of animals in nature. «She is a wedding photographer» tells you the job is taking pictures at weddings. The word before photographer tells you its special job.
fact: A photographer is a person who takes photographs, either as a job or as a hobby.
fact: The word can also mean the person who took one particular photo.
fact: «Wildlife photographer» means someone who takes pictures of animals in nature.
fact: In 1878 the photographer Eadweard Muybridge used a row of cameras to prove that a galloping horse has a moment with all four feet off the ground.
fact: Before you photograph someone, ask them first, and remember that a photographer should have permission to share pictures of children.
exercise: «The school photographer took our class picture on Monday.» Who took the class picture? | The bus driver | The class pet | *The school photographer | The head teacher
exercise: «Paparazzi are photographers who follow famous people to sell pictures.» What do paparazzi do? | Teach art in a school | *Follow famous people to take and sell pictures | Run a bakery and sell cakes | Cook dinner for celebrities
exercise: Why should you ask before you photograph someone? | Because photographers are always rude | Because they might be a famous photographer | Because it makes the camera work better | *They have a right to say whether their picture is taken and shared
test: «He is a wildlife photographer, and he spends weeks in the forest.» What does wildlife photographer mean? | A person who builds houses in the forest | A person who guides walkers through the hills | A teacher who studies trees | *Someone who takes pictures of animals in nature
test: «Checking can also show something is real: a named photographer and several big outlets are good signs.» What is a good sign that a photo is real? | A picture that is very old and faded | A picture with no name on it | Lots of likes online | *A named photographer and several big outlets
exam: What is a photographer? | *A person who takes photographs, as a job or a hobby | A person who draws pictures by hand | A person who sells cameras in a shop | A person who prints newspapers
